Emma 02 Emulator 
Copyright (C) 2007-2025 Marcel van Tongeren, core based on RCS Elf Emulator copyright (C) 2006 by Michael H Riley

ElfOS BIOS, Edt/Asm, Rc/Forth, Rc/Lisp, Rc/Basic and Bascom Copyright (C) 2004 by Michael H Riley

All included Quest software by Roger Pitkin is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported License. 

Super Basic V6.0 included with written permission and with updated origin info from Paul Messinger (see help pages on Quest Super Basic).

COSMAC ELF 2000 EPROM, Copyright (C) 2004 by Spare Time Gizmos 

The Sarnoff Collection at TCNJ - Chip 8, Coin Arcade, FRED 1, FRED 1.5, VIP and Studio II, III and IV SW. See readme and/or txt files for details

Hagley Museum and Library: Sarnoff/RCA Collection - Joseph A. Weisbecker’s archived manuscripts and materials - Accession 2464 -Box Number AVD B41: Chip 8, Coin Arcade, FRED 1, FRED 1.5, VIP and Studio II and III SW. See readme and/or txt files for details

The following libraries are licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL): wxWidgets, wxCurl, Blargg’s Blip Buffer library, libserialport, SDL (Simple DirectMedia Library) and SDL Audioin. Parts of EMULIB (by Bob Armstrong) are used for TU58 emulation and is licended under the GNU Affero General Public License. Curl and libcurl are licensed under a MIT/X derivate license.

Xbomber, Xchase, Xhorde, Xshoot, Xsnake, Xstinger, Xtrex and Xverbis games are build using: Crosslib library, 1802 devkit and the LCC1802 compiler
